{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#2510","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#2510","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#2510\",\"parent_revision\":\"7a3fe32fd2f157d328049d7b00c3c5e69db21c254082b2d09a0d0e784fc747ac\",\"root_revision\":\"7a3fe32fd2f157d328049d7b00c3c5e69db21c254082b2d09a0d0e784fc747ac\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: \\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: closed\\nadded: \\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAfter Phase 4 (task decomposition) completes in `dh:add-new-feature`, the skill instructs the orchestrator to call `backlog_update(selector=title, plan=P{id})` to link the new plan to the backlog item. In practice, this call is also written into the swarm-task-planner delegation prompt, so the subagent claims to have done it \u2014 but it silently fails to execute. The orchestrator then skips its own call because the subagent reported success.\\n\\nObserved during planning session for issue #2498: `swarm-task-planner` STATUS said \\\"linked to issue #2498\\\" but `backlog_view` returned `plan_path: null`. The orchestrator had to manually call `backlog_update(plan=P3e7e163d)` to fix it.\\n\\nImpact: Every session that goes through `dh:add-new-feature` leaves `plan_path` unset on the backlog item. Subsequent `/dh:work-backlog-item` invocations cannot route directly to `implement-feature` because `plan` field is empty. The work-backlog-item skill's \\\"if item already has a Plan field: invoke implement-feature\\\" shortcut never fires.\\n\\n**User-provided context**: The fix is for the orchestrator in `add-new-feature` SKILL.md to call `backlog_update(plan=...)` unconditionally after Phase 4 \u2014 never delegating it to the subagent. The subagent's self-report is not a reliable execution signal.\\n\\n## Fact-Check\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCLAIM: add-new-feature skill delegates backlog_update(plan=) to subagent instead of calling it from orchestrator \u2014 plan link silently fails\\nVERDICT: PARTIALLY REFUTED\\n\\nEVIDENCE:\\n\\n**Claim 1: \\\"Phase 4 of dh:add-new-feature SKILL.md instructs the orchestrator to call `backlog_update(selector=title, plan=P{id})` after swarm-task-planner completes.\\\"**\\n- Source: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md, lines 465-472\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-31\\n- Content excerpt:\\n  ```\\n  After the agent completes, write the plan path back to the backlog item:\\n  \\n  mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_update(\\n      selector=\\\"{title}\\\",\\n      plan=\\\"P{id}\\\"\\n  )\\n  ```\\n- VERIFIED \u2713 \u2014 The instruction is explicit, in Phase 4 section titled \\\"Task Decomposition\\\"\\n\\n**Claim 2: \\\"The swarm-task-planner delegation prompt template in the SKILL.md does NOT contain a `backlog_update(plan=...)` instruction.\\\"**\\n- Source: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md, lines 434-463 (delegation prompt template)\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-31\\n- Content: The delegation prompt block runs from line 435 (\\\"You are part of a team...\\\") through line 463 (closing backticks). No backlog_update call appears within this template. The prompt instructs the agent to \\\"Create the plan via sam_plan\\\" (line 444) but contains no MCP tool call to backlog_update.\\n- VERIFIED \u2713 \u2014 The delegation prompt delegates only task creation to the agent, not backlog state updates.\\n\\n**Claim 3: \\\"The work-backlog-item skill has an 'if item already has a Plan field: invoke implement-feature' shortcut.\\\"**\\n- Source: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/SKILL.md\\n  - Referenced in: start.md, line 29 (\\\"If item already has a Plan field: invoke `Skill(skill: \\\"dh:implement-feature\\\", args: \\\"{plan_address}\\\")` and stop\\\")\\n  - Implementation: locate.md, lines 41-45 (Step 1.4 \u2014 Extract Item Fields)\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-31\\n- Content excerpt (locate.md lines 41-45):\\n  ```\\n  If the item already has a `**Plan**:` field, extract the plan address from the YAML filename... \\n  Invoke immediately:\\n  \\n  Skill(skill: \\\"dh:implement-feature\\\", args: \\\"P{id}\\\")\\n  ```\\n- VERIFIED \u2713 \u2014 The shortcut exists and is documented as the proper routing when a plan already exists.\\n\\n**Claim 4: \\\"The current instruction wording 'After the agent completes' allows the orchestrator to skip the call if the subagent reports success.\\\"**\\n- Source: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md, line 465\\n- Retrieved: 2026-05-31\\n- Analysis: The instruction reads \\\"After the agent completes, write the plan path back to the backlog item:\\\" followed by the mandatory backlog_update call. The word \\\"write\\\" is an imperative instruction, not a conditional one. The instruction does not contain phrases like \\\"if not already written\\\", \\\"unless successful\\\", \\\"if the agent didn't\\\", or \\\"conditionally\\\" that would justify optional execution. The instruction is unambiguous and mandatory.\\n- REFUTED \u2717 \u2014 The wording does NOT allow skipping; it is a mandatory action that must occur after agent completion.\\n\\nCROSS_CHECK:\\n- Source: Implementation verification via work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/locate.md (lines 41-45)\\n- Finding: The work-backlog-item skill checks for an existing Plan field ONLY during the Locate phase (Step 1.4). If a plan exists, it skips directly to implement-feature. If no plan exists, it proceeds through grooming and planning phases. This confirms that the orchestrator IS responsible for writing the plan field back \u2014 if it does not, the item will not be routed to implement-feature on future invocations. The skip-to-implement-feature path depends on the plan field being present, which can only happen if the orchestrator successfully calls backlog_update(plan=...).\\n\\nEXPLANATION: Claims 1, 2, and 3 are all verified against source code. Claim 4 is refuted \u2014 the instruction wording at line 465 uses an imperative form (\\\"write\\\") that imposes a mandatory obligation, not a conditional one. The instruction does not support optional execution. The real bug is not ambiguous wording \u2014 the bug is that Phase 4's orchestrator instruction is NOT being executed (the orchestrator may be skipping it), which prevents the backlog item's plan field from being written. This causes the work-backlog-item skill's routing check in locate.md line 41 to fail on re-invocation, since the plan field is never populated.\\n\\nCITATION: |\\n  SOURCE: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md (lines 465-472, 434-463)\\n  SOURCE: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/locate.md (lines 41-45)\\n  SOURCE: /home/user/claude_skills/plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/start.md (line 29)\\n  VERIFIED_BY: Read tool on 2026-05-31\\n</div>\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Final: fix: add-new-feature skill delegates backlog_update(plan=) to subagent instead of calling it from orchestrator \u2014 plan link silently fails\\nDate: 2026-06-02\\nGoal: Eliminate ambiguous phrasing in add-new-feature Phase 4 so the orchestrator unconditionally calls backlog_update(plan=...) after swarm-task-planner completes, never delegating it.\\nConditions:\\n1. Source file `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` exists with Phase 4 backlog_update instruction at lines 465-471 | Snapshot: AVAILABLE \u2192 Final: AVAILABLE | Citation: Read SKILL.md lines 460-479 confirms lines 465-472 contain the mcp__plugin_dh_backlog__backlog_update(selector=\\\"{title}\\\", plan=\\\"P{id}\\\") block\\n2. Phase 4 delegation template does not explicitly contain backlog_update but \\\"After