Actions workflow references `add-new-feature`, `backlog_update(plan=)`, or plan-linking behavior.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` Phase 4 \\\"Plan Creation\\\" section \u2014 Phase 4 instructs the agent to call `sam_plan(action='create')` and optionally write disk output. It does NOT instruct the agent to call `backlog_update(plan=...)`. The delegation prompt in `add-new-feature/SKILL.md` must not delegate `backlog_update` to the swarm-task-planner \u2014 verify the fixed prompt removes any wording that the subagent might interpret as a license to claim plan linkage. | Risk: MEDIUM | Why: if the delegation prompt template (lines 436-463) contains any language that causes the subagent to self-report \\\"linked to issue #N\\\" in its STATUS, the orchestrator may still misread it post-fix; the prompt must clearly scope the subagent's responsibility to plan creation only\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` | Role: producer | Connection: Phase 4 instruction block (lines 465-472) is the root cause \u2014 orchestrator's `backlog_update` call is not unconditional | Action: CODE_CHANGE | Risk: HIGH | pattern: 'backlog_update'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/plan.md` | Role: consumer | Connection: Step 4.3 implements a parallel search-and-link path that compensates for the same bug; needs review for correctness and redundancy after fix | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM | pattern: 'backlog_update'\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/start.md` | Role: consumer | Connection: checklist Step 5.3 delegates to plan.md; accurate as long as plan.md is updated | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` | Role: consumer | Connection: entry precondition depends on plan_path being set; routing shortcut in work-backlog-item fires only when plan field is set | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/agents/swarm-task-planner.md` | Role: agent-instruction | Connection: Phase 4 Plan Creation \u2014 agent should not include backlog_update; delegation prompt must scope subagent responsibility to plan creation only | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_scenarios.py` | Role: test | Connection: tests backlog_update MCP tool but not the orchestrator-level unconditional call behavior; regression gap for the specific failure mode | Action: TEST_UPDATE | Risk: HIGH\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: P4_LINK node contracts table (line 410) attributes the call to the orchestrator; Status Advance note (line 428) describes expected behavior; verify actor attribution and unconditional constraint are clear | Action: CONTENT_UPDATE | Risk: MEDIUM\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-lifecycle.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: lines 261-266 document that the plan link is written by the orchestrator; verify remains accurate | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/workflow-architecture-diagram.md` | Role: documentation | Connection: Phase 1 diagram shows M4 backlog_update(selector, plan) node; structural accuracy unaffected by fix | Action: VERIFY_COMPATIBLE | Risk: LOW\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Risk Summary\\n\\n- Overall system risk: HIGH\\n- Highest-risk systems:\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 root cause; every session leaves `plan_path` unset until fixed; downstream routing (work-backlog-item implement-feature shortcut) silently never fires\\n  - `plugins/development-harness/tests/test_scenarios.py` \u2014 no test covers the orchestrator-skip failure mode; regression could silently re-enter after any future edit to Phase 4 delegation wording\\n- Main risk themes:\\n  - behavioral: orchestrator misreads subagent self-report as execution proof \u2014 silent data loss\\n  - verification: no automated test guards the unconditional call requirement\\n  - documentation: actor attribution and conditionality constraint could be made more explicit in lifecycle docs\\n- Scope expansion:\\n  - `work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/plan.md` Step 4.3 was discovered as a parallel rescue path addressing the same failure mode; this was not in the original item description and expands the review scope to confirm the two paths are consistent after fix\\n\\n---\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] Every code producer updated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every code consumer migrated or verified compatible\\n- [ ] Every affected test updated or new coverage added\\n- [ ] Every stale document updated\\n- [ ] Every affected config or CI path updated and validated\\n- [ ] Every affected agent or skill instruction updated\\n- [ ] Replacement or migration coverage gaps resolved\\n- [ ] Hidden transitive dependencies checked\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer relying on this plugin**, I want to **add-new-feature skill delegates backlog_update(plan=) to subagent instead of calling it from orchestrator \u2014 plan link silently fails** so that **the tool works correctly and reliably**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 plan P3e7e163d for issue #2498, 2026-05-30\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-05-30\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-05-31)\\n\\n### RT-ICA Assessment\\n\\n- Goal: Remove the trust-boundary violation in `dh:add-new-feature` Phase 4 so that `backlog_update(plan=...)` is always called by the orchestrator, never by or delegated to the subagent.\\n- Status: APPROVED\\n- AVAILABLE:\\n  - Fix locus is identified: SKILL.md lines 465-472 \u2014 verified by fact-check pass.\\n  - Root cause is verified: passive code block with no explicit actor assignment \u2014 confirmed REFUTED the \\\"ambiguous wording\\\" hypothesis.\\n  - Delegation template does NOT include `backlog_update` (lines 434-463) \u2014 verified; the call is only in the post-delegation block.\\n  - Fallback workaround exists: `work-backlog-item` locate.md lines 41-45 plan-field routing shortcut.\\n  - Observed instance documented: plan P3e7e163d for issue #2498, 2026-05-30.\\n  - Backlog MCP tool (`backlog_update`) is available to the orchestrator.\\n- DERIVABLE:\\n  - Regression test location: no `tests/test_scenarios.py` exists; the nearest test files are `tests/test_quality_gates.py` and `tests/test_quality_gate_integration.py`. Implementer must choose the correct test file or create one.\\n- MISSING:\\n  - None.\\n\\n### Artifact Classification\\n\\n- Primary artifact type: Bug fix (defect in LLM Prompt Engineering Artifact)\\n- Behavioral boundary: The orchestrator's execution trace after Phase 4 completes \u2014 specifically, whether `backlog_update(selector=..., plan=...)` appears as an orchestrator tool call in the session transcript, independent of what the swarm-task-planner subagent self-reports.\\n- Domain-semantic evaluation target: Acceptance criteria must verify that `plan_path` is non-null on the backlog item after Phase 4, that the orchestrator (not the subagent) issued the `backlog_update` call, and that `dh:work-backlog-item` can navigate to the plan without manual intervention.\\n\\n### Reproducibility\\n\\n1. Open a session with `dh:add-new-feature` active and a backlog item that has a linked GitHub issue (e.g. issue #2498).\\n2. Progress through Phases 1\u20133 normally until Phase 4 (task decomposition) completes.\\n3. Observe the swarm-task-planner subagent emit a STATUS self-report such as \\\"plan P{id} created and linked to issue #N\\\".\\n4. After Phase 4 completes, call `backlog_view(selector=\\\"#2498\\\", summary=True)` or inspect the per-item file.\\n5. Observe `plan_path: null` \u2014 the plan link was never written.\\n6. Confirm the orchestrator did not call `backlog_update(selector=..., plan=...)` independently; it accepted the subagent self-report as proof of execution.\\n\\n### Priority\\n\\n**Priority**: P1 \u2014 8/10 \u2014 silent data loss affecting every session that creates a feature plan through `add-new-feature`.\\n\\nThe plan link is infrastructure for the entire SAM pipeline: `work-backlog-item`, `implement-feature`, and milestone tooling all navigate from backlog item to plan via `plan_path`. A null `plan_path` breaks the handoff chain silently.\\n\\n**Effort**: S \u2014 change is scoped to one prose block in `add-new-feature/SKILL.md` (lines 465-472), plus a regression test entry. No architectural change required. No cross-plugin dependencies.\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\n- Blocks: `dh:work-backlog-item` plan-navigation shortcut (locate.md lines 41-45) \u2014 the shortcut resolves the plan path from the backlog item; when `plan_path` is null it cannot navigate.\\n- Blocks: `dh:implement-feature` \u2014 relies on `plan_path` to locate the SAM plan for dispatch.\\n- Blocks: `dh:complete-milestone` and milestone tooling \u2014 milestone plan aggregation reads plan links from backlog items.\\n- Misleads: orchestrator and human operators see \\\"plan linked\\\" in the subagent STATUS report and believe the link succeeded; no error is raised, no warning is emitted.\\n- Affects all sessions: every `add-new-feature` session that reaches Phase 4 produces a dangling plan with no backlog link, requiring manual repair via `backlog_update(plan=...)`.\\n- Observed instance: plan P3e7e163d for issue #2498 (2026-05-30) \u2014 `plan_path` remained null after Phase 4 completed.\\n\\n### Benefits\\n\\n- `dh:work-backlog-item` plan-navigation shortcut works immediately after Phase 4 completes, enabling uninterrupted session flow.\\n- `dh:implement-feature` can locate and dispatch the plan without manual intervention.\\n- Human operators and downstream agents can trust the backlog item's `plan_path` field as an accurate reflection of system state.\\n- Eliminates a class of silent trust-boundary violations where orchestrators accept subagent self-reports as proof of side-effect execution.\\n- Provides a regression test that catches future recurrences before they reach users.\\n\\n### Expected Behavior\\n\\nAfter Phase 4 (task decomposition) completes in `dh:add-new-feature`:\\n\\n1. The orchestrator \u2014 not the swarm-task-planner subagent \u2014 executes `backlog_update(selector=<backlog-item-title>, plan=<plan-id>)` unconditionally before proceeding to Phase 5.\\n2. The call succeeds and the backlog item's `plan_path` field is non-null.\\n3. A subsequent `backlog_view(selector=<title>, summary=True)` returns the correct `plan_path` value.\\n4. The swarm-task-planner subagent's STATUS self-report (\\\"plan created\\\") is treated as a status notification only \u2014 it does not substitute for the orchestrator's own `backlog_update` call.\\n5. If `backlog_update` returns an error, the orchestrator surfaces it and does not continue to Phase 5 until the link is established.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n1. After running `dh:add-new-feature` through Phase 4 on a test backlog item, call `backlog_view(selector=<item>, summary=True)` \u2014 `plan_path` is non-null and points to the created plan.\\n2. The swarm-task-planner subagent's output does NOT contain a `backlog_update` tool call \u2014 confirming the call is made by the orchestrator layer, not delegated to the subagent.\\n3. Given a session where the swarm-task-planner self-reports \\\"linked to issue #N\\\" but `backlog_update` has not been called by the orchestrator, `plan_path` remains null \u2014 confirming the self-report alone does not satisfy the link requirement. (Regression check for the root-cause failure mode.)\\n4. `dh:work-backlog-item` plan-navigation shortcut (locate.md lines 41-45) successfully resolves the plan path from the backlog item immediately after Phase 4 completes \u2014 no manual `backlog_update` call required.\\n5. A test scenario (in `tests/test_quality_gate_integration.py` or a new `tests/test_scenarios.py`) fails when `backlog_update(plan=...)` is omitted after Phase 4 and passes when it is present \u2014 providing an automated regression guard.\\n\\n### Resources\\n\\n| Type | Item |\\n|------|------|\\n| Skill | /dh:add-new-feature |\\n| Skill | /dh:work-backlog-item |\\n| Skill | /dh:implement-feature |\\n| Agent | @dh:swarm-task-planner |\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md (lines 465-472) |\\n| File | plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/locate.md (lines 41-45) |\\n| Backlog | #2498 \u2014 observed instance (plan P3e7e163d left unlinked 2026-05-30) |\\n| Docs | plugins/development-harness/CLAUDE.md \u2014 orchestrator trust boundary rules |\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` lines 465-472 \u2014 Phase 4 post-delegation block where `backlog_update(plan=...)` must be assigned an explicit actor (the orchestrator) and marked unconditional.\\n- `tests/test_scenarios.py` (or equivalent) \u2014 regression test for the orchestrator-skip failure mode is missing and must be added.\\n\\n### Dependencies\\n\\n- Depends on: None \u2014 all required context (SKILL.md location, backlog MCP tool) is AVAILABLE.\\n- Blocks: Any session using `dh:add-new-feature` Phase 4 that expects `plan_path` to be set on the backlog item afterward. Specifically blocks `dh:work-backlog-item` plan-navigation shortcut and `dh:implement-feature` plan dispatch for newly created plans.\\n\\n### Effort\\n\\nSmall \u2014 the fix is a single-file change to SKILL.md (lines 465-472): reword the post-delegation block to assign the `backlog_update(plan=...)` call explicitly to the orchestrator and mark it unconditional. The regression test addition to an appropriate test file is also bounded: one scenario covering the orchestrator-skip failure mode. Total scope is two files, no interface changes, no schema changes, no new dependencies.\\n\\n### Agent Instructions (instruct AI to use current interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` (Phase 4, lines 465\u2013471) \u2014 primary fix location; must add explicit \\\"ORCHESTRATOR NOTE: this call is always the orchestrator's responsibility \u2014 never delegate to the subagent\\\" annotation and optionally a verification step `backlog_view(selector=title, summary=True)` to confirm plan field is set before proceeding to Phase 5\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Consumers (read the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/locate.md::Step 1.4` (lines 41\u201344) \u2014 reads the `plan` field from the backlog item response; routes directly to `implement-feature` when `plan` is non-null; silently falls through to full planning workflow when `plan` is null (the failure mode this bug causes)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/work-backlog-item/references/workflows/work/start.md` (line 29) \u2014 documents the plan-field shortcut path (`If item already has a Plan field: invoke dh:implement-feature`) \u2014 no code change needed, will work correctly once producer is fixed\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Other References\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/implement-feature/SKILL.md` \u2014 invoked via the locate.md shortcut with `args: \\\"P{id}\\\"`; indirectly blocked when plan field is null because shortcut never fires; no change needed in this file\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md::Phase 5+` (lines 485+) \u2014 plan validation and subsequent phases rely on plan address `P{N}` being available from Phase 4 return; if backlog_update is called correctly, plan address is already recorded\\n\\n### Code \u2014 Producers (write the changed interface)\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md::Phase 4` (lines 465\u2013471) \u2014 orchestrator instruction to call `backlog_update(selector=title, plan=\\\"P{id}\\\")` after swarm-task-planner completes; fix must add explicit ORCHESTRATOR-MUST-CALL-UNCONDITIONALLY language and remove any delegation signal\\n\\n### Concerns\\n\\n| Category | Proposed Change Excerpt | Mission Source Violated | Citation |\\n|----------|------------------------|-------------------------|----------|\\n| \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 | \u2014 |\\n\\n### Configuration / CI\\n\\nNone identified.\\n\\n### Design Intent Alignment\\n\\nAlignment assessment: **ALIGNED**\\n\\n### Documentation (will become stale)\\n\\nNone identified \u2014 no documentation outside the SKILL.md specifically describes the orchestrator-vs-subagent boundary for the backlog_update call.\\n\\n### Ecosystem Completeness Checklist\\n\\n- [ ] `add-new-feature/SKILL.md` Phase 4 instruction updated: orchestrator-only annotation added, no delegation path\\n- [ ] Verify `swarm-task-planner` delegation prompt (SKILL.md lines 435\u2013463) does NOT contain `backlog_update` \u2014 if present, remove\\n- [ ] Regression test added to `tests/test_quality_gate_integration.py` or `tests/test_scenarios.py` asserting plan field is non-null after Phase 4\\n- [ ] `work-backlog-item/locate.md` requires no change \u2014 correctly reads plan field and routes when present\\n- [ ] `implement-feature/SKILL.md` requires no change\\n\\n### Impact Radius\\n\\n\\n\\n### Issue Classification\\n\\n**Type**: defect\\n\\n**Rationale**: This is a traceable failure with an identifiable cause chain. The orchestrator in Phase 4 delegates the `backlog_update(plan=...)` call to the swarm-task-planner subagent and then skips its own execution of the call based on the subagent's self-report. The subagent's `backlog_update` call fails silently (or does not execute), but the orchestrator never verifies completion independently. Decision tree: Q1 (not a typo) \u2192 Q2 (no recurring history) \u2192 Q3 (YES: traceable failure with identifiable cause) \u2192 **defect**.\\n\\n**Analysis Method**: 5-whys root-cause analysis via `/find-cause` skill\\n\\n**Scenario Target**: Orchestrator trusts subagent self-report without independent verification \u2192 Orchestrator executes `backlog_update(plan=...)` unconditionally after Phase 4, independent of subagent completion status\\n\\n### Root-Cause Analysis\\n\\n**Method**: 5-whys root-cause analysis (evidence-based from code review and issue description)\\n\\n**Evidence chain**:\\n\\n1. Observed failure: `backlog_view(selector=title)` returns `plan_path: null` after Phase 4 (task decomposition) completes in `dh:add-new-feature`\\n   - Evidence: Observed during planning session for issue #2498, 2026-05-30. SAM task plan P3e7e163d was created and the swarm-task-planner reported \\\"linked to issue #2498\\\", but the backlog item's `plan_path` field remained null.\\n\\n2. Why: The `backlog_update(selector=title, plan=P{id})` call was never executed or executed and failed silently\\n   - Evidence: Lines 468-471 of `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md` show the orchestrator is instructed to call `backlog_update` after Phase 4. The SAM MCP write-through pattern (lines 427-432) auto-registers the plan, but the metadata field linking is the orchestrator's responsibility.\\n\\n3. Why: The orchestrator skipped its own `backlog_update` call based on the subagent's self-report\\n   - Evidence: Lines 434-463 of `add-new-feature/SKILL.md` show that the same `backlog_update(plan=...)` instruction is also written into the swarm-task-planner delegation prompt. When the subagent's STATUS included \\\"linked to issue #2498\\\", the orchestrator interpreted this as proof that the call succeeded and did not execute its own call.\\n\\n4. Why: The subagent's `backlog_update` call failed silently, but the orchestrator had no mechanism to detect this\\n   - Evidence: The delegation prompt (lines 434-463) instructs the swarm-task-planner to create the plan via `sam_plan(action='create', issue={issue})`. The MCP auto-registers the `task-plan` artifact (line 476-477 note: \\\"sam_plan(action='create', issue={issue}) already auto-registers\\\"). However, the prompt does not include a `backlog_update` call \u2014 it only mentions plan creation. The orchestrator wrote the backlog_update instruction into the prompt but the subagent's actual prompt (as shown in lines 434-463) contains no such call. Result: subagent never executes `backlog_update`, reports creation success, orchestrator skips its own call believing it was already done.\\n\\n5. Root cause: The orchestrator delegates a critical side effect to a subagent but then trusts the subagent's self-report instead of executing the operation itself to verify completion\\n   - Evidence: Trust boundary violation \u2014 the orchestrator gives the subagent credit for an operation the subagent never executed, then skips the operation entirely. The orchestrator should execute `backlog_update(plan=...)` unconditionally after Phase 4, independent of any subagent report.\\n\\n**Root cause**: The orchestrator in `add-new-feature` SKILL.md relies on a subagent's self-report (\\\"linked to issue\\\") as proof that `backlog_update(selector=title, plan=P{id})` was executed, then skips its own execution of the call. When the subagent never actually calls `backlog_update`, the orchestrator never detects the failure and the plan remains unlinked.\\n\\n**Fix locus**: `plugins/development-harness/skills/add-new-feature/SKILL.md`, lines 465-471. The `backlog_update` call MUST be executed by the orchestrator unconditionally after Phase 4 completes, never delegated to the subagent. Remove `backlog_update` from the swarm-task-planner delegation prompt (if it appears there) and execute it in the orchestrator with explicit error handling.\\n\\n### Summary\\n\\n0 concerns identified \u2014 proposed change is consistent with product mission and historical direction. The proposal moves orchestrator responsibility for metadata linking (`backlog_update(plan=...)`) from subagent to orchestrator, aligning with Design Principle #1 (\\\"The harness owns the *process*; language plugins own the *specialists*\\\"). The orchestrator layer owns process transitions and metadata registration; delegating to subagent creates silent failures and breaks the artifact registration contract. Proposed change fixes an implementation error in current instruction by making plan linkage atomic and observable at the orchestrator layer, consistent with CLAUDE.md lines 13-19 and the Artifact Manifest System design (lines 154-167).\\n\\n### Systems Inventory\\n\\n| System | Role | Connection |\\n|---|---|---|\\n| `add-new-feature/SKILL.md` | Producer | Orchestrator that runs Phase 4 and must call `backlog_update(plan=...)` |\\n| `swarm-task-planner` agent | Plan creator | Creates SAM plan via `sam_plan(action='create')`; must NOT call `backlog_update` |\\n| `backlog_update` MCP tool | State writer | Writes `plan` field to backlog item; called by orchestrator only |\\n| `work-backlog-item/locate.md` | Consumer | Reads `plan` field; routes to `implement-feature` when non-null |\\n| `implement-feature/SKILL.md` | Downstream | Invoked by locate.md shortcut; cannot be reached when plan field is null |\\n\",\"digest\":\"771a7b84d1b9bd277f10ab398f27d0788cba06ae05536429a36814f51c81c58a\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABVCNLRA\"}"}